title The link that worked on one machine, and the guard reaching through what hid it
prompt Read KYRI and RADIANT_STYLE first, then REMEMBER and the itineraries and the top three log rows; Standfast on reds; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; deep-read one council-rota row; refresh REMEMBER; send often.
think Standfast first. Ran the whole standing roster cold before any new work -- 21 guards, 21 green, 0 red. The line was clear, so the lap could open constructively.
think Council rota row 2 -- Fire/Mars, cut and stop: Standfast, reds-first, the three depths of removal. The row handed the crux twice. Standfast says a lantern that fires twice becomes a loom; reds-first says every lantern that fires twice should become a self-halting machine. Three consecutive laps had found standing equipment behind the code it guards, which is a lantern firing three times.
think Then the row handed the red itself. Reading foundations/20260729-224828_reds-first-and-the-allocation.md for the rota, its header carried **Ledger:** [`../work-in-progress/REDS.md`]. Following it found a real 23,160-byte file. Asking git about it found nothing. `work-in-progress` is an UNTRACKED symlink to `crux` at the root of this pier, left by the 20260815 breach.
think The root is not the twenty-six missed references. The root is that no meter could see them. tools/living_docs_lint.rish tests a link target with `[ -e ]`, and a symlink satisfies `-e`, so a reference that breaks in every fresh clone read as a reference that works -- for eight days, with every guard green. Worse, the lint's own roster named work-in-progress/TASKS.md, so the guard was reaching through the artifact that blinded it.
think A census walking every tracked path found a second defect of the same family: pond/apps/corpora/waymark_green.md, a tracked symlink pointing at a waymark the 20260821.203103 fold had carried into waymarks/date/20260801/. dated_path_repoint.rish reads Markdown link text; a symlink's target lives in the filesystem rather than in any file body, so the repointer could never have seen it.
think The distinction that names both: a filesystem answers whether a path is here on this machine, and a reader who clones asks whether it is in the repository. Only the second is a promise, and *References are promises* is already house law.
obs The mechanism: tools/fixtures/tracked_link_scan.sh runs `git ls-files`, derives every ancestor directory with awk, reads the declared submodule paths out of .gitmodules with `git config -f .gitmodules --get-regexp`, and sorts the three into one known-path set. It then gates two readings at zero -- every tracked symlink (`git ls-files -s` filtered on mode 120000, target read with `readlink` and normalized by an awk pass that collapses `.` and `..`) resolves inside that set, and every relative Markdown link in a living document outside external-research/yonder and expanding-prompts/yonder resolves inside it. tools/tracked_link_witness.rish drives the scan and tools/fixtures/tracked_link_control.sh, asserting each verdict by name.
obs The narrowness is the design and it is proven rather than asserted. A link resolving NOWHERE passes free, because that duty already belongs to living_docs_lint and a second guard on one duty is two guards that can disagree. A document whose own basename carries a one-clock stamp passes free, because dated testimony keeps every reference it ever wrote and is resolved rather than rewritten. A symlink into vendor/ passes free, because that room is provisioned by `git submodule update` or by fetch_toolchain rather than tracked -- nineteen tracked symlinks point into vendor/zig-toolchain and every one is honest.
obs The control builds real git repositories rather than mimicking one. Seven behaviors on throwaway trees committed in a temporary pen: the clean tree free, an untracked target refused and counted, a stray symlink refused and counted, a vendor symlink free, a nowhere-link free, dated testimony free, and the yonder ratchet counted under its ceiling and refused once over it. Four refusals bitten, five honest readings left free.
obs The guard caught its own witness before it was committed. Its first roster run reported living_links_outside_tree=4, every one a link in crux/REDS.md pointing at the three files this lap had just written and not yet staged. That is the meter answering correctly -- a link to a file the repository does not carry is broken for a reader until the commit lands -- and `git add` closed it, since git ls-files reads the index.
obs The repointing raised the dated-path census by exactly one, and the cause was the control's own planted filename `20260101-000000_a-dated-note.md` being read as a real broken reference. That is the shape REDS %148's lap already paid for, so the repair was the shared exclusion list rather than a raised ceiling: tracked_link_control.sh joins banner_room_control.sh, room_bound_control.sh, and shipped_binary_claim_control.sh as instrument rather than field, and the census returned to the exact 192 baseline.
obs Booking two rows carried crux/REDS.md to 27,549 bytes against its 24,576 bound, so rows %150-%151 folded to crux/archive/ with the doorway line written in the same act, every relative link repointed one level deeper and checked to resolve on disk. The monotone guard then refused three times over -- headline total, span, and remainder each one row behind the spine -- which is the third lap running that a ledger guard has corrected a hand.
obs Adding a witness left both generated pages one behind, exactly as REDS %152 named. The pre-commit wall refreshes them in the commit that moves them; the roster ran before the commit, so both were regenerated by hand this lap -- front door now reading fascia 41 and 1,653 witnesses over 1,890 modules, library index at 38 rows.
obs What this does not prove: that a link points at the RIGHT file, only that it points at a file the repository carries. And 219 links still stand in the two deferred yonder silos, held under a ceiling that only ever falls and repaired on touch rather than swept, because a sweep across a deferred shelf would bury the enforced zero in noise.
loom witness=tracked_link scan_wall_s=42 tracked_paths=13907 tracked_symlinks=263 living_md=646 links_enforced=0 links_ratcheted=219
loom roster=standing_equipment guards=22 green=22 red=0 wall_s=170
file tools/fixtures/tracked_link_scan.sh the meter -- builds the fresh-clone path set from git ls-files, ancestor dirs, and .gitmodules, then gates symlinks and living links at zero
file tools/fixtures/tracked_link_control.sh seven behaviors on throwaway git repositories -- four refusals bitten, five honest readings left free
file tools/tracked_link_witness.rish the rung -- drives scan and control, asserts every verdict by name
file crux/standing-equipment.kyri tracked_link seated as the roster's twenty-second guard
file crux/REDS.md rows %153 and %154 booked and closed, headline corrected to the measured 154, rows %150-%151 folded out under bound
file crux/archive/REDS-the-roster-and-its-first-run-rows-150-151.md the fold, links repointed one level deeper and checked on disk
file tools/fixtures/dated_path_exclusions.sh tracked_link_control.sh joins the shared list as instrument rather than field, census back to the 192 baseline
file tools/fixtures/living_docs_lint_roster.sh repointed to crux/ so the lint stops reaching through the untracked symlink
file pond/apps/corpora/waymark_green.md the one dangling tracked symlink in 13,907 paths, repointed to the folded waymark home
file crux/REMEMBER.md Now refreshed to the tracked-link work, roster count raised to twenty-two
recommend keep-going the ladder arc's queue is unchanged and waiting -- rests_path leads the free-absolutely reading at 250 over eleven rungs, confer_words holds the queue's free head at 294 over forty-three rungs priced at forty-three import re-exports, and answered_by still leads by return at 330 costing sixty-eight openings. Beside it this lap opens a sharper question than the one it closed: an untracked artifact at the root of a working tree silenced a whole class of guard for eight days without ever appearing in a diff, so the honest next meter asks which OTHER guards read the filesystem where they mean to read the repository -- living_docs_lint's own broken-link duty still tests with `[ -e ]`, and it is one of several.
